# Card hover clearance

When creating or adjusting a page whose cards use an upward hover transform, leave enough gap above the cards that the lift and shadow do not overlap the bar or panel above.

Check this on card grids that sit under a header or a preview, especially in portrait (`@media (orientation: portrait)`).

- Keep the resting cards far enough below the bar or panel that `translateY(-2px)` and the card shadow still clear that edge. Aim for at least about 10px between the lifted card top and the element above.
- If a parent clips with `overflow: hidden`, put the gap inside that parent (padding) so the lift is not cut off.
- Keep next and back actions inside the viewport. Do not add a document scrollbar to make room; let the cards shrink to fit when the height is short.

```css
.tool-tile.is-ready:hover {
  transform: translateY(-2px);
}

.card-panel {
  padding-top: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
```
